1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,550
[Disclaimer: Characters, behaviors,
places, organizations, professions,

2
00:00:02,570 --> 00:00:05,030
and events shown
in the series are entirely fictional,

3
00:00:05,050 --> 00:00:07,510
solely for the purpose of entertainment,
with no intention to instruct

4
00:00:07,530 --> 00:00:09,990
or promote any kind of behavior;
viewer discretion is advised]

5
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:14,810
Xinxin!

6
00:00:16,710 --> 00:00:17,790
I'm sorry.

7
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:19,600
One day,

8
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:22,090
you'll find your own umbrella, Xinxin.

9
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:24,520
No matter how hard it rains,

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,610
you won't need to find shelter.

11
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:29,500
Sweet dreams.

12
00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:36,070
Come with me.

13
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:37,680
I'll buy it for you.

14
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:40,100
Consider it a good-luck charm
from a feng shui master.

15
00:00:41,190 --> 00:00:43,480
Will love ever find its way to me?

16
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:44,560
It would.

17
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:46,010
You won't even see it coming.

18
00:01:45,850 --> 00:01:46,610
Hey.

19
00:01:47,270 --> 00:01:48,320
Why are you spacing out?

20
00:01:49,490 --> 00:01:49,890
Huh?

21
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:51,480
Are you thinking about
what happened last night?

22
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:53,610
I'm... I'm not.

23
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:56,170
Come on, let's go inside

24
00:01:56,190 --> 00:01:57,200
and have breakfast.

25
00:01:58,330 --> 00:01:59,690
Oh? Let's go.

26
00:02:01,910 --> 00:02:03,200
Do you

27
00:02:03,830 --> 00:02:05,690
really eat like this every day?

28
00:02:10,270 --> 00:02:12,290
Have you ever heard of...

29
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:13,600
Thai barbecue,

30
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:14,770
pizza,

31
00:02:15,060 --> 00:02:17,040
or even cream cheese mochi?

32
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,500
Of course I have.

33
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:21,440
I just don't eat them.

34
00:02:24,330 --> 00:02:25,400
Afraid of gaining weight?

35
00:02:27,710 --> 00:02:28,710
I'm not.

36
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:31,900
I just want to take care of my health

37
00:02:32,510 --> 00:02:34,810
because my mom only has me now.

38
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:37,480
I want to take care of her for a long time.

39
00:02:38,910 --> 00:02:39,910
Whoa...

40
00:02:41,050 --> 00:02:42,070
You're making me

41
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:44,300
feel guilty now.

42
00:02:46,810 --> 00:02:49,410
But you take good care of
your mom too, don't you?

43
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:51,910
And you don't have these every day.

44
00:02:52,510 --> 00:02:53,190
Am I right?

45
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:55,690
Yeah, not every day.

46
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:57,700
Who's gonna have these every day?

47
00:02:57,720 --> 00:02:59,800
Here, have some of my oranges.

48
00:03:01,090 --> 00:03:02,890
Try some. It’s easy to eat.

49
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:11,010
This one’s easy to eat.

50
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:12,220
It's tasty, too.

51
00:03:15,790 --> 00:03:17,990
Just don't think about it.
Don't overthink it.

52
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:21,120
The vibe of the house is...

53
00:03:21,290 --> 00:03:22,430
A little old-fashioned.

54
00:03:22,450 --> 00:03:24,580
No, I mean, it looks more luxurious.

55
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:31,200
Hi.

56
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:33,700
So pretty...

57
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:39,290
What? Where are you going?

58
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:42,590
Hello, Ms. Lada.

59
00:03:53,910 --> 00:03:55,510
Is there an emergency?

60
00:03:56,410 --> 00:03:57,190
There is.

61
00:03:58,500 --> 00:03:59,720
What is it?

62
00:04:00,010 --> 00:04:01,170
I wanted to see you.

63
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:04,160
That's not an emergency.

64
00:04:04,730 --> 00:04:05,920
For me, it is.

65
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:08,370
Or I wouldn't have come
all the way here to see you.

66
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,950
I'm totally speechless.

67
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,300
Let's have dinner tonight.

68
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,800
It's not work-related, so don't worry.

69
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,580
If it's not work-related,

70
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:22,170
that's even more worrying.

71
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:23,610
Why is that?

72
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:27,200
Is there something about me
you don't trust?

73
00:04:27,550 --> 00:04:28,920
It's not like that.

74
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:31,000
Well, I was just thinking...

75
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:32,580
What else would we have to talk about

76
00:04:32,970 --> 00:04:35,120
if not work?

77
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,480
Of course!

78
00:06:20,620 --> 00:06:21,770
Oyl!

79
00:06:21,790 --> 00:06:22,810
Oh, sis?

80
00:06:25,330 --> 00:06:27,180
If someone you've just met

81
00:06:27,490 --> 00:06:29,380
invites you out for a meal,

82
00:06:29,590 --> 00:06:31,010
do you think they're up to something?

83
00:06:33,790 --> 00:06:34,610
Definitely!

84
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:36,570
What is it?

85
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:38,400
It's either an investment opportunity

86
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:40,440
or insurance they're trying to sell you.

87
00:06:41,510 --> 00:06:43,190
- What?
- Be serious.

88
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:45,600
How would I know?

89
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,320
Why don't you ask them yourself?

90
00:06:47,970 --> 00:06:50,120
You sure ask a lot
about other people's business.

91
00:06:53,530 --> 00:06:54,590
Hm...

92
00:06:55,730 --> 00:06:56,850
Anyway,

93
00:06:57,590 --> 00:06:59,490
we haven't heard from Soul, have we?

94
00:07:00,510 --> 00:07:01,660
I wonder how she's doing.

95
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:02,520
See?

96
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:04,600
I just said that, and you're asking again.

97
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:08,210
I don't know.

98
00:07:08,230 --> 00:07:10,210
I guess they're fine, though.

99
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:11,820
Otherwise, she would've called us

100
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:13,310
to vent about it already.

101
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:15,390
Yeah, you're right...

102
00:07:15,410 --> 00:07:16,030
Mm.

103
00:07:16,170 --> 00:07:17,790
Alright, let's get back to work.

104
00:07:18,900 --> 00:07:20,720
You shouldn't be the one saying that.

105
00:07:21,810 --> 00:07:23,100
You left me here alone.

106
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:29,060
I agree with the feng shui master

107
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:31,120
that we shouldn't start foundation piling yet.

108
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:32,640
Could you say that again?

109
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:35,960
Actually, it's still unclear
whether foundation piles are necessary.

110
00:07:36,070 --> 00:07:38,670
We need an engineer
to conduct a soil investigation first.

111
00:07:38,690 --> 00:07:40,610
because it's a structural matter.

112
00:07:41,970 --> 00:07:45,000
I have to apologize to everyone...

113
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,620
for lashing out yesterday as well.

114
00:07:48,610 --> 00:07:49,800
There's nothing to worry about.

115
00:07:49,820 --> 00:07:52,820
As long as you and the feng shui master

116
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:54,890
understand each other well, I'm happy.

117
00:07:56,420 --> 00:07:56,990
Oh?

118
00:07:57,010 --> 00:07:59,510
I have to head back to Bangkok now

119
00:07:59,610 --> 00:08:01,090
because something urgent has come up.

120
00:08:01,110 --> 00:08:03,080
But don't worry,

121
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:05,000
I've got dinner all taken care of.

122
00:08:05,250 --> 00:08:06,390
You shouldn't miss it.

123
00:08:06,410 --> 00:08:07,890
If you need anything,
feel free to contact my secretary.

124
00:08:07,910 --> 00:08:08,730
Thank you.

125
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:09,790
My pleasure.

126
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:12,190
You can use Madam's name

127
00:08:12,210 --> 00:08:13,600
for the 6:00 P.M. reservation.

128
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:15,510
- Thank you, Madam.
- Thank you.

129
00:08:15,530 --> 00:08:17,290
I hope you both enjoy dinner tonight.

130
00:08:17,310 --> 00:08:18,390
I'll get going now.

131
00:08:18,410 --> 00:08:19,110
Of course.

132
00:08:19,130 --> 00:08:20,110
Okay.

133
00:08:20,610 --> 00:08:21,770
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

134
00:08:21,790 --> 00:08:23,090
Goodbye.

135
00:08:30,690 --> 00:08:31,990
Want to go for a walk?

136
00:08:37,970 --> 00:08:40,210
And why did you suddenly believe me?

137
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,190
No.

138
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:43,960
I didn't believe you.

139
00:08:44,710 --> 00:08:47,710
I talked to a senior of mine
who's an engineer.

140
00:08:49,110 --> 00:08:51,320
Did they say we shouldn't do the piling?

141
00:08:52,630 --> 00:08:53,510
No.

142
00:08:53,530 --> 00:08:56,030
They said this is an engineer's job.

143
00:08:56,050 --> 00:08:57,290
I should stay out of it.

144
00:08:57,310 --> 00:08:58,820
They'll handle
the structural work themselves.

145
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:00,310
Really?

146
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,190
He chewed me out for that.

147
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:07,320
How did you know piling wasn't necessary?

148
00:09:08,830 --> 00:09:10,100
Well...

149
00:09:20,210 --> 00:09:21,900
the topsoil there isn't quite shallow.

150
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:24,710
You know about this stuff, too?

151
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:27,690
A feng shui master
should know some of this, too.

152
00:09:27,710 --> 00:09:28,710
Whoa...

153
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:31,770
I'm an architect,
but even I don't know this much.

154
00:09:32,030 --> 00:09:33,310
That's alright.

155
00:09:33,340 --> 00:09:34,830
You're an architect, Soul,

156
00:09:34,850 --> 00:09:36,070
not an engineer.

157
00:09:36,090 --> 00:09:37,290
It's alright if you don't know.

158
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:41,410
Uh...

159
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,810
what are you smiling about?

160
00:09:44,010 --> 00:09:45,180
Can you call me that again?

161
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:47,440
Call you what?

162
00:09:48,510 --> 00:09:49,810
You called me "Soul."

163
00:09:55,610 --> 00:09:57,810
Where are you going, Xinxin? Wait for me!

164
00:09:58,500 --> 00:09:59,210
Xinxin!

165
00:09:59,490 --> 00:10:00,730
Come on, wait for me.

166
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:03,920
What?

167
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:05,290
Why are you pulling me?

168
00:10:07,290 --> 00:10:09,020
Let's have dinner together tonight, okay?

169
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:14,590
Mm.

170
00:10:15,490 --> 00:10:17,590
Madam Waen already booked us a table.

171
00:10:20,850 --> 00:10:22,300
Come on, let's go back.

172
00:10:31,190 --> 00:10:32,190
I'm sorry.

173
00:10:34,510 --> 00:10:36,300
Just hold my hand properly.

174
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:37,590
You don't have to pull me.

175
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:23,700
Am I late, or are you just early?

176
00:11:24,730 --> 00:11:26,000
I got here early

177
00:11:26,540 --> 00:11:28,400
because I wanted to see you sooner.

178
00:11:33,180 --> 00:11:34,000
Wine?

179
00:11:35,330 --> 00:11:36,120
Sure.

180
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:57,530
What made you

181
00:11:57,610 --> 00:11:59,210
ask me out to dinner?

182
00:12:00,700 --> 00:12:02,600
I wanted to get to know you better,

183
00:12:03,140 --> 00:12:05,230
but not as your client.

184
00:12:06,910 --> 00:12:07,580
Why?

185
00:12:08,790 --> 00:12:10,300
You really don't realize

186
00:12:11,450 --> 00:12:12,810
I'm into you?

187
00:12:15,230 --> 00:12:16,400
I know.

188
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,320
You're so obvious.

189
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:21,610
You are, too.

190
00:12:22,310 --> 00:12:23,640
Otherwise,
you wouldn't be here with me.

191
00:12:27,090 --> 00:12:28,300
Aren't you put off by me?

192
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:32,300
You're not off-putting at all.

193
00:12:33,140 --> 00:12:34,300
Besides,

194
00:12:34,590 --> 00:12:36,880
I've had my eye on you

195
00:12:37,010 --> 00:12:38,500
ever since we first met.

196
00:12:44,340 --> 00:12:45,290
What about you?

197
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:47,880
Are you really into me,

198
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:49,710
or are you just interested?

199
00:12:52,450 --> 00:12:55,380
Well, I don't know if I like you or not,

200
00:12:56,110 --> 00:12:57,910
but I'm very interested.

201
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:05,290
I'm dying to know

202
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:07,800
if I can make you like me.

203
00:14:16,400 --> 00:14:17,530
Did you come looking for me?

204
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,360
Mm.

205
00:14:22,380 --> 00:14:24,690
I couldn't find you
when I came out of the bathroom.

206
00:14:26,190 --> 00:14:26,800
Well...

207
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,580
you took a long shower,

208
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:30,110
so I went out for a walk.

209
00:14:31,730 --> 00:14:33,320
Why are you wearing your hair down today?

210
00:14:35,630 --> 00:14:36,290
Well...

211
00:14:36,740 --> 00:14:37,900
it goes well with my outfit today.

212
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:41,980
It really suits your outfit.

213
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:45,370
What did you just say?

214
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:48,900
No.

215
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:50,340
Nothing.

216
00:14:51,550 --> 00:14:53,210
I heard you say something.

217
00:14:53,590 --> 00:14:55,030
I bet you said

218
00:14:55,050 --> 00:14:57,610
it doesn't suit me,
or that I look ugly in it.

219
00:15:00,810 --> 00:15:01,810
You look pretty...

220
00:15:15,410 --> 00:15:16,700
I'm hungry.

221
00:15:16,820 --> 00:15:17,890
Let's go grab something.

222
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:21,400
"Pretty..."

223
00:15:28,390 --> 00:15:29,390
You...

224
00:15:29,790 --> 00:15:31,000
can eat these, right?

225
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:33,490
There aren't any veggies in them.

226
00:15:34,270 --> 00:15:35,390
It's just one day.

227
00:15:35,410 --> 00:15:37,730
Since we're at the beach,
we might as well have some seafood.

228
00:15:41,030 --> 00:15:41,990
But...

229
00:15:42,530 --> 00:15:43,810
I'm a bit bummed.

230
00:15:44,100 --> 00:15:46,110
I thought they were gonna peel the shrimp

231
00:15:46,130 --> 00:15:47,630
and crack the crabs for me.

232
00:15:48,690 --> 00:15:50,510
The best part about eating seafood

233
00:15:50,530 --> 00:15:52,630
is getting to do it yourself, you know.

234
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:55,710
I can't be bothered.

235
00:15:56,290 --> 00:15:56,840
Oh.

236
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:58,920
I forgot to wash my hands.

237
00:15:59,150 --> 00:16:00,600
I just got done playing in the sand.

238
00:16:01,290 --> 00:16:02,490
Hold on, I'm gonna wash them.

239
00:16:19,590 --> 00:16:20,280
Wait...

240
00:16:20,570 --> 00:16:21,910
did you peel them for me?

241
00:16:24,090 --> 00:16:25,200
I didn't.

242
00:16:25,510 --> 00:16:27,100
I just asked the staff.

243
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:29,420
Oh...

244
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:41,030
What's the matter?

245
00:16:41,290 --> 00:16:42,560
Are you allergic to seafood?

246
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:44,710
No, I'm not.

247
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:45,880
Um...

248
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:48,650
I think it's the sea breeze.

249
00:16:48,910 --> 00:16:51,300
It gets colder as the sun starts to set.

250
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:53,200
Whoa.

251
00:16:53,850 --> 00:16:55,400
That shrimp is huge.

252
00:16:55,420 --> 00:16:57,800
What if you get sick?

253
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:00,610
I rarely get sick.

254
00:17:00,830 --> 00:17:02,720
You're the one who should be careful.

255
00:17:16,930 --> 00:17:17,630
What?

256
00:17:18,730 --> 00:17:22,210
You peeled them for me
until your hands were bleeding.

257
00:17:24,210 --> 00:17:25,210
Put your spoon down!

258
00:17:25,650 --> 00:17:26,330
Come on.

259
00:17:28,990 --> 00:17:31,810
You can just admit you did it, you know.

260
00:17:31,830 --> 00:17:33,800
It won't kill you to admit it.

261
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,490
You'll get too comfortable
and start making me do everything.

262
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,210
I'm not that bad.

263
00:17:41,510 --> 00:17:42,800
You are that bad.

264
00:18:00,810 --> 00:18:01,990
Done.

265
00:18:06,810 --> 00:18:07,810
Thank you.

266
00:18:14,130 --> 00:18:15,200
Let's dig in.

267
00:18:16,310 --> 00:18:17,480
Let me dip mine, too.

268
00:18:23,550 --> 00:18:24,600
This is so good!

269
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:28,280
All for you. Finish them all, okay?

270
00:18:28,300 --> 00:18:29,300
Can I?

271
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:39,210
I'm so full!

272
00:18:39,740 --> 00:18:40,980
Are you okay?

273
00:18:41,610 --> 00:18:42,920
Or do I have to carry you?

274
00:18:43,990 --> 00:18:45,110
Can you?

275
00:18:46,690 --> 00:18:48,250
My back's gonna break for sure.

276
00:18:49,220 --> 00:18:51,500
I'm not that heavy.

277
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:54,970
So...

278
00:18:54,990 --> 00:18:56,560
what are you gonna do when we get back?

279
00:18:56,590 --> 00:18:57,590
Go straight to bed?

280
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:00,120
I'll probably do some work first.

281
00:19:01,250 --> 00:19:02,960
You still have to do it?

282
00:19:03,310 --> 00:19:05,300
I'm most productive at night,

283
00:19:05,790 --> 00:19:07,130
but I don't usually stay up late.

284
00:19:07,150 --> 00:19:08,510
I'm not really a fan of it.

285
00:19:10,010 --> 00:19:12,000
You're taking such good care of yourself.

286
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:13,820
How could Auntie Tai
still be worried about you?

287
00:19:14,250 --> 00:19:15,940
My mom is just like that.

288
00:19:16,250 --> 00:19:18,390
I'm all she has left now,

289
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:22,910
since my dad passed away
after working so hard for our family.

290
00:19:23,610 --> 00:19:26,220
So my mom doesn't want me
to end up like him.

291
00:19:27,510 --> 00:19:28,620
That's why...

292
00:19:29,570 --> 00:19:31,990
you're taking good care
of yourself for her, right?

293
00:19:34,890 --> 00:19:36,420
For now, yes.

294
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:40,680
But someday, I might meet someone...

295
00:19:41,700 --> 00:19:44,490
who makes me
want to live a long life with them.

296
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:49,480
You used to tell me...

297
00:19:49,780 --> 00:19:52,800
love will find its way to me
before I even realize it, right?

298
00:19:54,740 --> 00:19:55,620
Mm.

299
00:19:56,710 --> 00:19:57,820
Yeah.

300
00:19:59,530 --> 00:20:00,810
I think...

301
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:02,410
it's getting closer.

302
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:27,020
You're the first person
I've ever brought to my place, you know.

303
00:20:28,230 --> 00:20:29,700
Should I feel honored?

304
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:32,600
What? You should!

305
00:20:33,010 --> 00:20:35,280
since you're my first.

306
00:20:36,110 --> 00:20:38,030
You're my first, too.

307
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:42,010
But I've never been to your place, though.

308
00:20:43,710 --> 00:20:45,200
I mean...

309
00:20:45,590 --> 00:20:48,180
you're the first woman I've ever liked.

310
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:55,920
Come on.

311
00:20:58,510 --> 00:21:00,150
- Hey...
- Hey, where's your key?

312
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:08,300
What are you doing?

313
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,900
Nothing. I was just checking my work.

314
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,510
Then why are you hiding it?

315
00:21:15,210 --> 00:21:17,280
I think I caught a glimpse of it.

316
00:21:17,420 --> 00:21:20,550
It's the same color
as the shirt I wore today.

317
00:21:20,730 --> 00:21:21,660
Nothing, Xinxin.

318
00:21:21,670 --> 00:21:23,690
I told you it's just some work.

319
00:21:25,220 --> 00:21:26,290
Really?

320
00:21:26,840 --> 00:21:27,790
Mm.

321
00:21:29,410 --> 00:21:30,410
Okay.

322
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:34,400
Let me see it.

323
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:37,290
No, it's just my work.

324
00:21:37,310 --> 00:21:38,710
- I really saw it.
- My work...

325
00:21:38,910 --> 00:21:40,800
I told you it's work. It's not... Hey...

326
00:21:41,610 --> 00:21:42,520
Hey!

327
00:22:01,410 --> 00:22:02,590
- Ow!
- You pervert!

328
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,070
What, Xinxin?

329
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:08,920
I haven't even done anything.

330
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:12,610
So does that mean
you'll do it if I get carried away?

331
00:22:14,520 --> 00:22:15,310
What?

332
00:22:16,010 --> 00:22:17,960
That means you might get carried away?

333
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:19,320
- Hey!
- Ow!

334
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:21,900
It hurts. Why did you hit me, Xinxin?

335
00:22:22,840 --> 00:22:23,840
Good.

336
00:22:23,860 --> 00:22:24,800
Maybe now you'll remember!

337
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:25,790
Ow...

338
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,400
Xinxin.

339
00:23:00,260 --> 00:23:01,280
Xinxin...

340
00:23:01,710 --> 00:23:04,110
What? I'm gonna sleep.

341
00:23:05,740 --> 00:23:06,790
Sweet dreams.

342
00:23:55,420 --> 00:23:57,800
Hey, are you
secretly taking pictures of me?

343
00:23:59,810 --> 00:24:00,600
Mm.

344
00:24:01,900 --> 00:24:03,410
Let me see. Do I look pretty?

345
00:24:06,810 --> 00:24:07,810
Yeah.

346
00:24:09,600 --> 00:24:10,200
Whoa!

347
00:24:10,700 --> 00:24:12,000
You took really nice pictures.

348
00:24:12,020 --> 00:24:13,100
Can you send them to me?

349
00:24:15,510 --> 00:24:17,100
You're even prettier
in person than in the photo.

350
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:25,690
It's...

351
00:24:25,910 --> 00:24:27,100
It's getting too hot now.

352
00:24:27,490 --> 00:24:28,290
We should get going.

353
00:25:09,190 --> 00:25:09,810
Oh!

354
00:25:10,390 --> 00:25:12,330
This is my favorite song.

355
00:25:13,010 --> 00:25:18,090
♫Because I feel too much for you♫

356
00:25:18,610 --> 00:25:25,360
♫With all my heart,
but I know it's impossible♫

357
00:25:25,380 --> 00:25:28,040
Lada, wanna sing? It's so much fun.

358
00:25:28,060 --> 00:25:29,060
Oh, this song!

359
00:25:29,080 --> 00:25:31,410
This is also my favorite, Ms. Lada!

360
00:25:31,630 --> 00:25:32,900
If you don't mind.

361
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:38,320
♫The Siam tulips bloom,
but soon they will wither♫

362
00:25:38,340 --> 00:25:40,710
♫I'm still waiting just the same,♫

363
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:44,440
♫Whose woman have you become?♫

364
00:25:47,160 --> 00:25:52,380
♫The Siam tulips bloom,
but soon they will wither♫

365
00:26:50,210 --> 00:26:51,310
Same clothes.

366
00:27:22,620 --> 00:27:23,310
Hey.

367
00:27:24,300 --> 00:27:25,300
Are you up already?

368
00:27:26,490 --> 00:27:28,690
There's nothing in your fridge, Mim.

369
00:27:29,710 --> 00:27:30,910
How about a fried egg?

370
00:27:32,620 --> 00:27:33,620
"Mim..."

371
00:27:34,800 --> 00:27:36,000
Do you even remember anything?

372
00:27:39,800 --> 00:27:41,400
Gosh. Hey, you...

373
00:27:41,500 --> 00:27:42,790
- Don't go limp on me.
- I'm sleepy...

374
00:27:42,810 --> 00:27:43,920
You have to help me, too.

375
00:27:44,110 --> 00:27:44,810
Ouch...

376
00:27:46,600 --> 00:27:49,180
What’s with all that “you and I”?

377
00:27:49,500 --> 00:27:50,810
Well, just "You and I."

378
00:27:50,820 --> 00:27:52,590
I'm tired of "Ms." this and that.

379
00:27:54,390 --> 00:27:57,200
Oh...

380
00:28:04,200 --> 00:28:05,490
Lada...

381
00:28:07,190 --> 00:28:09,610
Do you really like me...

382
00:28:09,960 --> 00:28:12,200
or are you just messing with me?

383
00:28:21,710 --> 00:28:23,120
Well...

384
00:28:24,400 --> 00:28:25,600
It's...

385
00:28:27,390 --> 00:28:28,120
Um...

386
00:28:52,300 --> 00:28:54,100
I didn't answer you last night

387
00:28:54,620 --> 00:28:55,680
because you were too drunk.

388
00:28:58,500 --> 00:28:59,990
As for whether

389
00:29:00,010 --> 00:29:03,400
I really like you
or I'm just messing around...

390
00:29:05,220 --> 00:29:06,120
It's fun.

391
00:29:10,200 --> 00:29:11,960
It's fun being with you.

392
00:29:17,990 --> 00:29:19,500
So, I think...

393
00:29:22,200 --> 00:29:24,620
I actually might really like you, Mim.

394
00:30:01,920 --> 00:30:04,020
Thank you for dropping me off.

395
00:30:05,900 --> 00:30:08,500
Aren’t you even going to invite me in?

396
00:30:09,550 --> 00:30:10,600
Nope.

397
00:30:11,110 --> 00:30:12,300
My mom isn't home yet.

398
00:30:12,490 --> 00:30:14,380
I'm afraid I won't be safe.

399
00:30:15,410 --> 00:30:16,310
Xinxin.

400
00:30:16,510 --> 00:30:17,910
If you keep saying things like this,

401
00:30:17,930 --> 00:30:20,360
I'll start thinking
you're actually scared of me.

402
00:30:20,520 --> 00:30:22,890
It's not like that.
I'm not scared of you.

403
00:30:22,910 --> 00:30:24,310
I was just joking.

404
00:30:25,610 --> 00:30:26,520
Okay.

405
00:30:26,700 --> 00:30:28,400
At least I know...

406
00:30:29,140 --> 00:30:30,400
you care about me.

407
00:30:32,100 --> 00:30:33,100
See you later.

408
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:36,360
There's no reason for us
to meet again.

409
00:30:37,910 --> 00:30:38,820
Oh,

410
00:30:39,160 --> 00:30:40,410
there are plenty of reasons.

411
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:43,200
I'll head inside now.

412
00:30:43,820 --> 00:30:44,560
Bye-bye.

413
00:30:47,520 --> 00:30:48,520
Well,

414
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:50,100
and...

415
00:30:51,350 --> 00:30:52,580
don't stay up late.

416
00:30:54,290 --> 00:30:55,680
Or Auntie Tai will be worried about you.

417
00:30:59,200 --> 00:31:00,480
Come on, let me help.

418
00:31:03,930 --> 00:31:04,920
I'll close it for you.

419
00:31:04,940 --> 00:31:06,000
Go on inside.

420
00:31:36,300 --> 00:31:37,910
Gosh, Soul, are you smiling?

421
00:31:57,250 --> 00:32:01,180
[Xinxin]

422
00:32:04,160 --> 00:32:05,180
Hm...

423
00:32:05,600 --> 00:32:08,100
You took so many pictures of me,
Miss Architect.

424
00:32:09,350 --> 00:32:10,800
Since you took so many,

425
00:32:10,820 --> 00:32:12,810
I guess I should charge you, huh?

426
00:32:14,040 --> 00:32:15,770
Shouldn't you be thanking me

427
00:32:15,790 --> 00:32:17,900
for the photos you can post on Instagram?

428
00:32:18,340 --> 00:32:21,570
Oh, thank you.

429
00:32:24,700 --> 00:32:26,180
Sweet dreams, Xinxin.

430
00:32:29,560 --> 00:32:30,590
Not yet.

431
00:32:50,110 --> 00:32:51,110
[New post]

432
00:32:51,130 --> 00:32:52,600
She took some pretty cute pictures, huh?

433
00:33:01,610 --> 00:33:02,370
[Share]

434
00:33:19,760 --> 00:33:21,640
[JR CONSTRUCTION]

435
00:33:31,610 --> 00:33:32,280
Weird.

436
00:33:32,630 --> 00:33:33,590
So weird.

437
00:33:34,090 --> 00:33:35,010
True.

438
00:33:35,200 --> 00:33:37,100
She's usually as expressionless as a robot.

439
00:33:37,720 --> 00:33:39,200
The moment she got back from
Prachuap Khiri Khan,

440
00:33:40,500 --> 00:33:41,580
she started smiling.

441
00:33:43,300 --> 00:33:44,900
Come on, what are we waiting for?

442
00:33:44,920 --> 00:33:45,910
Let's go.

443
00:33:48,590 --> 00:33:49,700
- Soul!
- Soul!

444
00:33:50,450 --> 00:33:51,280
Gosh...

445
00:33:51,360 --> 00:33:52,650
You scared the heck out of me.

446
00:33:52,670 --> 00:33:54,120
Popping up out of nowhere like ghosts.

447
00:33:54,410 --> 00:33:55,600
Wow...

448
00:33:56,510 --> 00:33:58,930
Was there something good at
Pran Buri or what?

449
00:33:58,950 --> 00:34:00,310
- Yeah.
- Exactly.

450
00:34:00,700 --> 00:34:01,520
Why do you ask?

451
00:34:01,810 --> 00:34:02,620
Well,

452
00:34:02,640 --> 00:34:05,150
you walked into our office
with this creepy smile.

453
00:34:05,170 --> 00:34:07,390
- Yeah.
- Plus, you're wearing your lucky color.

454
00:34:07,410 --> 00:34:08,760
- That's right.
- Yeah.

455
00:34:09,920 --> 00:34:11,210
Is it that obvious?

456
00:34:11,500 --> 00:34:12,790
Yeah!

457
00:34:12,920 --> 00:34:15,530
Since when did you
start believing in this stuff?

458
00:34:15,550 --> 00:34:17,110
I thought you said it was nonsense.

459
00:34:17,890 --> 00:34:19,490
It doesn't hurt to believe a little, does it?

460
00:34:19,510 --> 00:34:21,280
I've got a client meeting today,

461
00:34:22,130 --> 00:34:23,550
so it's nice
to have something to believe in.

462
00:34:23,570 --> 00:34:24,460
Oh...

463
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:25,980
Really?

464
00:34:27,110 --> 00:34:29,190
You're acting suspicious, huh?

465
00:34:29,320 --> 00:34:31,960
Stop teasing me and get
the work ready for the client.

466
00:34:32,110 --> 00:34:33,700
If you two keep teasing me,

467
00:34:33,720 --> 00:34:35,350
I'll rat you out to the boss

468
00:34:35,370 --> 00:34:36,720
and tell him
you've got nothing better to do.

469
00:34:36,750 --> 00:34:37,400
Hey!

470
00:34:37,820 --> 00:34:40,590
Alright, you can take it from here, Mim.

471
00:34:40,610 --> 00:34:44,310
- I'd better...get back to work.
- Hey.

472
00:34:44,340 --> 00:34:45,580
Hey, I'm...

473
00:34:45,600 --> 00:34:46,770
I'm busy now.

474
00:34:46,790 --> 00:34:48,450
- I'm off. Bye-bye.
- Hey, Mim... Mim!

475
00:34:48,470 --> 00:34:50,270
Mim! Your card!

476
00:34:50,290 --> 00:34:52,080
- Mim. I'm out.
- Hey!

477
00:35:21,700 --> 00:35:22,790
Hello, Xinxin.

478
00:35:23,560 --> 00:35:24,590
Miss Architect.

479
00:35:26,190 --> 00:35:29,000
I'm waiting to meet a client.
I'll be done in half an hour.

480
00:35:29,490 --> 00:35:30,710
Is something up, Xinxin?

481
00:35:30,870 --> 00:35:33,500
Well... never mind. That’s all.

482
00:35:35,190 --> 00:35:36,110
Hold on!

483
00:35:36,230 --> 00:35:37,110
Xinxin!

484
00:35:43,500 --> 00:35:45,510
What's the matter, Xinxin?

485
00:35:51,890 --> 00:35:54,260
Something urgent came up.
Can you handle the client for me?!

486
00:35:54,280 --> 00:35:55,700
I'll talk to the boss about this later.

487
00:35:56,030 --> 00:35:57,580
Hey, Soul!

488
00:35:57,600 --> 00:35:58,600
Wait!

489
00:36:01,180 --> 00:36:01,880
Uh...

490
00:36:30,390 --> 00:36:33,400
Could you move back a little bit?

491
00:36:33,610 --> 00:36:34,880
I'm a little uncomfortable.

492
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:39,920
Sorry, my eyesight isn't that great,

493
00:36:39,940 --> 00:36:41,560
so I have to look at things up close.

494
00:36:42,700 --> 00:36:43,580
Oh...

495
00:36:43,900 --> 00:36:44,590
Well...

496
00:36:45,420 --> 00:36:47,830
I'll show it to you once it's done.

497
00:36:49,300 --> 00:36:50,090
Alright.

498
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:07,600
How about this?

499
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:09,690
Once we're done with work,

500
00:37:09,900 --> 00:37:11,240
why don't we go out to eat together?

501
00:37:11,630 --> 00:37:14,710
Just think of it as a little celebration
for working together.

502
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:16,820
I'm afraid I can't.

503
00:37:19,010 --> 00:37:20,010
It won't take long.

504
00:37:22,790 --> 00:37:23,890
I don't think she can.

505
00:37:27,790 --> 00:37:28,790
Who are you?

506
00:37:29,390 --> 00:37:30,490
How did you get into my house?!

507
00:37:31,510 --> 00:37:33,410
I'm Feng Shui Master Xinxin's girlfriend.

508
00:37:47,300 --> 00:37:48,410
Even matching outfits, huh?

509
00:37:53,200 --> 00:37:55,200
I didn't think the timing
would be this perfect.

510
00:38:00,890 --> 00:38:02,300
You can let go of me now.

511
00:38:04,410 --> 00:38:06,490
Why did you say that to him?

512
00:38:07,210 --> 00:38:08,290
Say what?

513
00:38:09,720 --> 00:38:11,000
Well...

514
00:38:12,190 --> 00:38:13,350
Telling him

515
00:38:13,370 --> 00:38:14,780
that I'm your girlfriend?

516
00:38:15,750 --> 00:38:16,810
Mm.

517
00:38:17,950 --> 00:38:19,590
Would he have let you go

518
00:38:19,790 --> 00:38:21,510
if I hadn't said that to his face?

519
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:24,910
You can tell just by looking at his face
that he's not trustworthy.

520
00:38:31,290 --> 00:38:33,980
Thank you...for coming.

521
00:38:39,420 --> 00:38:40,420
Hey.

522
00:38:40,730 --> 00:38:42,080
What about your work?

523
00:38:42,300 --> 00:38:44,200
You said you have a client meeting today.

524
00:38:45,390 --> 00:38:46,510
Don't worry.

525
00:38:46,900 --> 00:38:48,610
You're more important, Xinxin.

526
00:38:54,610 --> 00:38:57,100
I'm sorry for causing you trouble.

527
00:38:58,230 --> 00:38:59,920
I told you it's okay.

528
00:38:59,940 --> 00:39:01,320
Don't worry about it.

529
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:04,960
But if you feel bad,

530
00:39:06,490 --> 00:39:08,690
why don't you treat me to a meal?

531
00:39:12,690 --> 00:39:13,380
Mm.

532
00:39:16,930 --> 00:39:17,930
Mm...

533
00:39:18,900 --> 00:39:20,010
You promise?

534
00:39:33,740 --> 00:39:36,330
Hello. A table for two?

535
00:39:36,590 --> 00:39:37,380
Yes.

536
00:39:37,510 --> 00:39:39,290
Um... excuse me...

537
00:39:39,310 --> 00:39:41,430
you two are a couple, right?

538
00:39:41,690 --> 00:39:43,100
No, we're not!

539
00:39:44,840 --> 00:39:47,910
Oh, I saw you wearing matching outfits,
so I assumed you were.

540
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:49,430
My apologies.

541
00:39:49,550 --> 00:39:52,200
Today is the owner's wedding anniversary,

542
00:39:52,220 --> 00:39:54,020
so we're offering
a special 20% discount on food

543
00:39:54,040 --> 00:39:55,760
for all couples.

544
00:39:55,780 --> 00:39:57,020
We are.

545
00:39:57,040 --> 00:39:59,490
Well...we had a little spat,

546
00:39:59,510 --> 00:40:01,720
but we're actually dating.

547
00:40:04,010 --> 00:40:07,110
Oh, alright. Right this way, please.

548
00:40:10,810 --> 00:40:11,810
What are you doing?

549
00:40:15,220 --> 00:40:16,010
What?

550
00:40:16,190 --> 00:40:19,290
You told my client
we were a couple earlier,

551
00:40:19,310 --> 00:40:20,400
so I'm just doing the same.

552
00:40:20,490 --> 00:40:22,580
They’re even offering 20% off.

553
00:40:22,600 --> 00:40:23,670
Who wouldn't want that?

554
00:40:25,700 --> 00:40:26,890
I'm blushing here.

555
00:40:29,190 --> 00:40:29,690
Come on.

556
00:40:30,040 --> 00:40:31,040
Gosh!

557
00:40:47,610 --> 00:40:49,620
Why are you
wearing your hair down again today?

558
00:40:50,310 --> 00:40:52,000
Don't tell me...

559
00:40:52,020 --> 00:40:53,400
it goes with this outfit, too.

560
00:40:55,290 --> 00:40:57,290
It really does match, though.

561
00:40:58,520 --> 00:40:59,520
Oh, really?

562
00:40:59,610 --> 00:41:01,490
I thought you let your hair down

563
00:41:01,610 --> 00:41:02,670
because I said

564
00:41:02,700 --> 00:41:04,910
you looked pretty
with it down the other day.

565
00:41:13,120 --> 00:41:14,420
It's not like that.

566
00:41:14,910 --> 00:41:16,690
I look pretty
no matter how I wear my hair.

567
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:21,320
That's true.

568
00:41:39,120 --> 00:41:40,960
How did you know about this restaurant?

569
00:41:41,120 --> 00:41:43,190
I bet you bring girls here
on dates all the time.

570
00:41:43,590 --> 00:41:45,080
There's nothing but couples.

571
00:41:46,190 --> 00:41:48,200
Why would I bring girls here all the time?

572
00:41:49,270 --> 00:41:50,010
Well...

573
00:41:50,290 --> 00:41:51,930
this place looks so romantic.

574
00:41:51,950 --> 00:41:53,030
It's perfect for a date.

575
00:41:55,710 --> 00:41:56,710
In that case...

576
00:41:58,010 --> 00:42:00,110
I guess you're the first woman

577
00:42:00,300 --> 00:42:02,000
I've ever brought here on a date.

578
00:42:16,350 --> 00:42:18,490
You don't have to do this for me.

579
00:42:18,510 --> 00:42:20,210
I won't tell Auntie Tai.

580
00:42:20,940 --> 00:42:22,210
What I'm doing

581
00:42:22,710 --> 00:42:24,190
is because I want to do it for you.

582
00:42:24,810 --> 00:42:26,690
Not because anyone told me to.

583
00:42:29,210 --> 00:42:30,210
Well...

584
00:42:30,610 --> 00:42:32,300
you must be quite the flirt, then.

585
00:42:33,120 --> 00:42:33,890
Hm?

586
00:42:35,240 --> 00:42:36,040
Well...

587
00:42:36,300 --> 00:42:38,270
you look after me, take care of me,
pay attention to me,

588
00:42:38,390 --> 00:42:40,180
and sometimes you even spoil me.

589
00:42:40,200 --> 00:42:42,000
That's what you'd call flirting.

590
00:42:44,600 --> 00:42:46,010
So, can I?

591
00:43:04,200 --> 00:43:05,720
You can call me anytime.

592
00:43:08,120 --> 00:43:08,960
Hm?

593
00:43:09,230 --> 00:43:11,390
If you ever run into
something you're not okay with

594
00:43:11,730 --> 00:43:13,300
and don't know who to call,

595
00:43:14,010 --> 00:43:15,800
you can always call me.

596
00:43:16,620 --> 00:43:18,680
You can even use my name
and say I'm your girlfriend.

597
00:43:23,190 --> 00:43:24,640
You, too.

598
00:43:25,160 --> 00:43:25,880
Hm?

599
00:43:26,830 --> 00:43:28,820
You can use my name, too.

600
00:43:29,000 --> 00:43:31,900
Just in case you get caught
dating around or something,

601
00:43:31,920 --> 00:43:34,710
you can use my name as an excuse.

602
00:43:36,140 --> 00:43:38,070
Hm... I don't think

603
00:43:38,420 --> 00:43:40,230
I'd ever need to use your name.

604
00:43:42,360 --> 00:43:44,360
Because lately,

605
00:43:45,210 --> 00:43:46,590
you're the only one in my life.

606
00:43:48,400 --> 00:43:50,090
So there's no need to use your name.

607
00:44:21,320 --> 00:44:23,770
So Soul is your architect?

608
00:44:23,800 --> 00:44:26,160
Let's talk about these two.

609
00:44:26,180 --> 00:44:27,770
Hey, how could you not tell me?!

610
00:44:27,790 --> 00:44:28,480
I'm shocked!

611
00:44:29,120 --> 00:44:31,100
Are you really sick?

612
00:44:31,120 --> 00:44:32,660
Why don't we share a bed every night?

613
00:44:32,690 --> 00:44:33,480
What?

614
00:44:33,720 --> 00:44:35,780
Where do we go from here?

615
00:44:38,230 --> 00:44:39,760
When we really like someone,

616
00:44:40,690 --> 00:44:42,400
what does it feel like?

617
00:44:43,410 --> 00:44:46,290
Try placing your hand
on your heart, like this.

618
00:44:52,890 --> 00:44:54,390
You're calling so early. What's up?

619
00:44:55,000 --> 00:44:57,490
What's today's lucky color?

620
00:44:57,730 --> 00:44:59,910
There's plenty of information online,
isn't there?

621
00:45:00,100 --> 00:45:02,910
I wanted to ask an expert
to make sure I got it right.

622
00:45:06,400 --> 00:45:09,690
Light blue and dark blue for career success.

623
00:45:09,710 --> 00:45:11,790
Just don't wear black or gray.

624
00:45:12,540 --> 00:45:13,590
That will bring bad luck.

625
00:45:20,900 --> 00:45:22,300
Alright.

626
00:45:22,330 --> 00:45:25,190
Understood, Miss Feng Shui.
